      "text": "Given the expression $\\left\\lceil-\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{4}}\\right\\rceil$, we first simplify the term inside the ceiling function.\n\nThe square root of $\\frac{49}{4}$ can be simplified as:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{4}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{49}}{\\sqrt{4}} = \\frac{7}{2}.\n\\]\n\nSo the expression becomes:\n\\[\n\\left\\lceil -\\frac{7}{2} \\right\\rceil.\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to evaluate $-\\frac{7}{2}$. Since $\\frac{7}{2}$ is greater than 3 but less than 4, we have:\n\\[\n-\\frac{7}{2} = -3.5.\n\\]\n\nThe ceiling function $\\left\\lceil x \\right\\rceil$ rounds $x$ up to the nearest integer. Since $-3.5$ is between $-3$ and $-2$, and it is closer to $-3$ than to $-2$, we have:\n\\[\n\\left\\lceil -3.5 \\right\\rceil = -3.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-3}.\n\\]",
