      "text": "To solve the problem \\(\\left\\lceil -\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{4}} \\right\\rceil\\), we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Evaluate the inner expression \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{4}}\\):**\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{\\frac{49}{4}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{49}}{\\sqrt{4}} = \\frac{7}{2}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Subtract this value from 0 to get \\(-\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{4}}\\):**\n   \\[\n   -\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{4}} = -\\frac{7}{2}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Find the ceiling of \\(-\\frac{7}{2}\\):**\n   The ceiling function \\(\\left\\lceil x \\right\\rceil\\) returns the smallest integer greater than or equal to \\(x\\).\n\n   Here, \\(x = -\\frac{7}{2} = -3.5\\).\n\n   The smallest integer greater than or equal to \\(-3.5\\) is \\(-3\\).\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-3}\n\\]",
